@startuml
!theme cyborg
skinparam backgroundColor #111827
skinparam defaultFontColor #F3F4F6
title Version 1 = MVP — distinct system responsibilities (owner decision November 4)
skinparam backgroundColor #111827
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam wrapWidth 180

left to right direction
actor "Private user\nOwner/admin created or invited" as U
actor "Employer viewer\nResume link authorization" as V
rectangle "Resumefolio core" as CORE #164E63 {
 rectangle "Dashboard / private profile\nTailored resumes / portfolio\nCover letters / manual applications" as C
 rectangle "PDF / protected sharing\nExplicit publish and selection" as S
 folder "My Files & Media\nPrivate same-server bytes\nSupported uploads / YouTube links" as F
 C --> S : explicit preview / select / apply\nseparate publish confirmation
 F --> S : only selected material\nauthorized direct / range retrieval
}
rectangle "ProjectForge — separate system\nReal repositories / permissions\nClone / fetch / pull / push\nFile-history / issues / simple Kanban\nEngine / database / placement undecided" as PF #164E63
rectangle "Future — after MVP\nPrivate communications system via API\nPersonal Gmail / Google Calendar\nAdvanced Git review / releases\nAdvanced backlog / Sprints\nYAML execution / deployment / AI" as FUT #164E63
U --> C : own permitted resources
V --> S : selected resume / media / PDF\nno owner login
C <--> PF : authenticated user-scoped API\nno shared database assumed
actor "Native Git client" as G
G --> PF : real authorized Git transport\ncommits normally in client
FUT -[hidden]-> PF
legend bottom
 Upload does not publish. Core uploads remain on the same Resumefolio server.
 Future communications: explicit per-user/account consent; admin cannot read users' mail.
 Logical responsibility only; no physical ProjectForge topology or runtime verification claimed.
endlegend
@enduml
